# CCCI modem-init, device-owned.
#
# Derived from stock /vendor/etc/init/init.cccimdinit.rc, which this tree used
# to extract verbatim. It is owned here for the same reason init.volte_imcb.rc
# is: the one difference from stock has to be visible in a diff rather than
# buried in a blob_fixup sed.
#
# That difference: the MD3 half is gone. MD3 is MediaTek's C2K/CDMA2000
# protocol stack and this chassis has no CDMA radio. Measured on the handset:
#
#   /sys/kernel/ccci/md_en            E-D-D-D-D (1->5)   only MD1 enabled
#   /proc/config.gz                   CONFIG_MTK_MD3_SUPPORT=0
#   ro.vendor.mtk_protocol1_rat_config Lf/Lt/W/T/G       no C2K
#   ro.vendor.mtk_md3_support         unset
#   /dev/ccci2_* /dev/ccci3_*         do not exist
#   init.svc.ccci3_mdinit             stopped
#
# `ccci_mdinit 2` therefore ran at every boot, found nothing, and exited. The
# two mkdirs it left behind (/mnt/vendor/nvdata/md3 and /data/vendor/md3) stayed
# empty; the nvdata one is still dated from the factory image.
#
# The `insmod` lines stock carries here are commented out in stock too: ccci is
# built into this kernel. They are simply dropped rather than carried as dead
# comments.

on post-fs-data
    # Modem related device nodes
    mkdir /mnt/vendor/nvdata/md  0770 root system

    chown radio radio /sys/kernel/ccci/boot

    mkdir /data/vendor/ccci_cfg 0770 system radio
    restorecon /data/vendor/ccci_cfg

service ccci_mdinit /vendor/bin/ccci_mdinit 0
    user system
    group radio system
    class core
    oneshot
